<$fill $name="body">

!! Link the new tiddler to the drop target

The usual setup: the new tiddler's `parent` field names the tiddler you dropped on. Create this tiddler in your wiki:

```
title: $:/config/rimir/drop-attach/actions/link-parent
tags: $:/tags/rimir/drop-attach/action

<$action-setfield $tiddler=<<new>> parent=<<target>>/>
```

Any field works the same way, e.g. `attachment-of=<<target>>`.

!! Add more fields

```
title: $:/config/rimir/drop-attach/actions/fields
tags: $:/tags/rimir/drop-attach/action

<$action-setfield $tiddler=<<new>> caption=<<filename>> tags="attachment"/>
```

!! List the target in a field of the target

```
title: $:/config/rimir/drop-attach/actions/list-on-target
tags: $:/tags/rimir/drop-attach/action

<$action-listops $tiddler=<<target>> $field="attachments" $subfilter="[<new>]"/>
```

!! Open images below the drop target, keep PDFs closed

`$:/config/rimir/drop-attach/open-filter`:

```
[all[]] :filter[get[type]prefix[image/]]
```

(Core `is[image]` would also match PDFs.)

!! Keep attachments in one folder per day

`$:/config/rimir/drop-attach/title-filter`:

```
[<now YYYY-0MM-0DD>addprefix[attachments/]addsuffix[/]addsuffix<filename>]
```

</$fill>
</$transclude>
"},"$:/plugins/rimir/drop-attach/doc/faq":{"title":"$:/plugins/rimir/drop-attach/doc/faq","created":"20261104090000000","modified":"20261104090000000","rdt.hub-category":"tools","rdt.hub-category-name":"Tools","rdt.hub-order":"4","rdt.order":"5","rdt.plugin-key":"drop-attach","rdt.plugin-name":"drop attach","rdt.plugin-subtitle":"Drop or paste binary files onto a tiddler","rdt.section":"FAQ","type":"text/vnd.tiddlywiki","text":"<$transclude $tiddler="$:/plugins/rimir/doc-template/templates/page">
<$fill $name="body">

!! Q: Why is nothing linked after a drop?

The plugin links nothing by itself. Add an action tiddler (see //Examples → Link the new tiddler to the drop target//).

!! Q: I dropped a Markdown file and got the import dialog.

On purpose: text files are tiddler content, not attachments, and go to the normal import. Only binary types are attached.

!! Q: Paste does nothing / says to select a tiddler.

Click into the tiddler you want to paste into (the thin bar on its left edge shows it is selected), then paste. The selected tiddler must be visible. A paste into a text editor is left to the editor.

!! Q: Does it need a server?

No. The file is stored in the wiki. On a Node.js server wiki TiddlyWiki saves it as a real file next to its `.meta`; in a single-file wiki it stays embedded until you extract it.

!! Q: My file type is attached as application/octet-stream.

TiddlyWiki does not know it. Add a line `<mime type> <.extension>` to `$:/config/rimir/drop-attach/extra-types` and restart.

!! Q: Can I drop on something other than story tiddlers?

Yes: tag a tiddler <<tag "$:/tags/rimir/drop-attach/target">> with a `selector` and the `title-attribute` that holds the title (see //Reference → Drop targets//).

</$fill>
</$transclude>
